  "notes": "MF DOOM  (as producer; Metal Fingers' Special Herbs, Operation: Doomsday)\n\nTECHNIQUE (sourced)\n- DOOM called the SP-404 \"a nice, flexible machine\"; he used an MPC1000 with JJ OS and Pro\n  Tools; \"On a regular loop, I turn the quantize off\"; \"I consider myself a drummer\" (Wax\n  Poetics). He had an MPC60 in the KMD era (Ambrosia For Heads).\n- Gear specific to Special Herbs or Operation: Doomsday: unconfirmed. The SP-303 + Vinyl Sim\n  setup here follows the brief and the SP-303 lineage (MusicTech), not a DOOM interview.\n\nTHIS TEMPLATE\nSP-303 Sampler for loops (press Vinyl Sim for the dust); a second Sampler with SP Radio\nTuning for TV and cartoon drops; a drum rack swung at 54% (nearer the grid than Dilla):\nThe drum rack plays one-shots synthesized for these templates (CC0, no recordings), in the voice of the machine each channel is named for, with a starter beat in the pattern; replace them with your own samples for the real machine. Vocal with a fast compressor and some Overdrive.\n\nMIX NOTES\n- Loops loud, drums under them; the vocal dry and close (no delay, short room).\n- Drum Bus: a hard built-in compressor, CHOWTapeModel \"Old MPC\"; Music Bus CHOWTapeModel\n  \"Dirtier Cassette\".\n- Master: CHOWTapeModel \"Old Tape\", Lemon Limiter; -12 to -10 LUFS.\n- Loudness: streaming plays back near -14 LUFS integrated (Spotify), so a louder master is turned down; keep true peak below -1 dBTP.\n\nCOVERAGE\nMedium: the setup is right for the sound; the documented DOOM gear (MPC1000, SP-404) is not\nmodelled beyond the Sampler. The drums are synthesized one-shots, not samples of the machines.\n\nSOURCES\nWax Poetics \"MF DOOM Interview: Behind the Mask\"; Ambrosia For Heads (2018); MusicTech SP-303\nfeature; Spotify for Artists, \"Loudness normalization\" (support.spotify.com/us/artists/article/loudness-normalization).\n\nFREE PLUG-INS (download them before opening the template; a missing one keeps its slot)\n- CHOWTapeModel (GPL-3.0): https://chowdsp.com/products.html\n\nSETUP (written from this template)\nTempo 84 BPM, 4/4, key Fmin, cycle bars 1-4.\n\nTracks\n- Loops (SP-303) (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Sampler (SP-303 model): no effect; quantize 16; pad grade lofi\n- Drums (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Drum Bus\n    instrument: Channel Rack (synthesized one-shots of the template samples: Kick = kick-acoustic.wav, Snare = snare-acoustic.wav, Closed Hat = hat-acoustic.wav, Open Hat = openhat-acoustic.wav, Rim = rim.wav, Shaker = shaker.wav)\n    region: Step Sequencer pattern with a starter beat (13 steps on), swing 54% (MPC terms), 6 rows = the rack's channels\n- TV / Cartoon Drops (Instrument, -8 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Sampler (SP-303 model): effect RadioTuning on, CTRL 1-3 = 50%, 40%, 60%; quantize 16; pad grade lofi\n- Vocal (Audio, +0 dB) -> Vocal Bus\n    strip FX: Compressor (Threshold -20, Ratio 4, Attack 0.5, Release 60, Make-up 3)\n    strip FX: Overdrive (Drive 9, Tone 6000, Level -4, Mix 0.5)\n    send: Reverb (bus 4) at -24 dB\n\nBuses (the n-th Aux strip listens to bus n)\n- Drum Bus (bus 1): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Old MPC\"; Compressor (Threshold -24, Ratio 8, Attack 1, Release 80, Make-up 6)\n- Music Bus (bus 2): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Dirtier Cassette\"\n- Vocal Bus (bus 3): Compressor (Release 150, Make-up 2)\n- Reverb (bus 4): Space D (Dry -96, Wet 0, Decay 0.6, Decay Curve 1, IR \"00.5s Small Room\")\n- Delay (bus 5): Tape Delay (Time 95, Feedback 0.1, Tone 3500, Mix 1)\n\nStereo Out\n- built-in effects: Channel EQ (High -2); Compressor (Threshold -12, Ratio 2, Attack 30, Release 200)\n- plug-ins (after the built-in effects): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Old Tape\"; Lemon Limiter: gain +2.5 dB, ceiling -1 dB, other settings default\n\nBring your own samples: no recordings are included.\n",
